IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `miles-card-domain`
IMPORT `miles-card`

§ `The issuers' own worked examples, run through the composer`

-- ===========================================================================
-- THE CASE SUITE. Every assertion below is taken from a WORKED EXAMPLE the
-- issuer printed in its own document: an illustration table inside a T&C, or
-- a numbered answer in that card's FAQ. Nothing here is our arithmetic about
-- what a clause ought to mean. Where the issuer gave a points TOTAL for an
-- amount, the assertion is on the PER-DOLLAR RATE that total implies, and the
-- comment shows the division.
--
-- WHY THE EXAMPLES AND NOT THE CLAUSES. The issuer modules encode the
-- clauses; asserting the clauses back at them would only restate the
-- encoding. An illustration is different: it is the issuer's own application
-- of its own rules to a concrete charge, and it is the one part of the
-- document the drafter had to make come out right. So it is evidence
-- INDEPENDENT of how we read the operative words, which is what a case suite
-- is for.
--
-- EVERYTHING GOES THROUGH THE COMPOSER. Each assertion calls
-- `the rate on` card cardholder month txn, never an issuer rule directly, so
-- the suite also exercises the dispatch in `miles-card.l4` and would catch a
-- card wired to the wrong module.
--
-- HOW TO READ A FAILURE. A failing assertion here is a FINDING, not a bug in
-- the assertion: either the encoding disagrees with the issuer's own
-- illustration, or the illustration is not reachable through the fields the
-- domain carries. Do not edit an assertion to match the answer it got.
--
-- THE LAST SECTION IS DELIBERATELY BRITTLE. Two FAQs contradict their own
-- T&Cs. The assertions there state what the T&C says, because the T&C
-- governs; they are written so that a later change that follows the FAQ
-- instead trips a test rather than passing silently.
--
-- Document ids are the ones in source/source-bundle.json. Clause numbers are
-- the issuer's own.
-- ===========================================================================


§§ `The cardholders`

-- A Citi Rewards holder has no field in this domain that its T&C makes
-- operative: Citi conditions nothing on a standing fact about the customer.
GIVETH A Cardholder
`a Citi Rewards cardholder` MEANS Cardholder WITH
    `Solitaire preferred rewards categories`               IS EMPTY
    `yuu account linked to the card`                       IS FALSE
    `HSBC Everyday Global Account deposits ADB this month` IS 0
    `PAssion membership registered and card linked in yuu` IS FALSE

-- hsbc-revolution-reward-points-tnc cl.7.1(ii)(b) and the cl.9 table split
-- every HSBC answer on one number: the Deposits ADB in the Eligible EGA
-- Account for the calendar month. These two cardholders are the table's two
-- rows.
GIVETH A Cardholder
`an HSBC cardholder below the deposits tier` MEANS Cardholder WITH
    `Solitaire preferred rewards categories`               IS EMPTY
    `yuu account linked to the card`                       IS FALSE
    `HSBC Everyday Global Account deposits ADB this month` IS 0
    `PAssion membership registered and card linked in yuu` IS FALSE

GIVETH A Cardholder
`an HSBC cardholder at the deposits tier` MEANS Cardholder WITH
    `Solitaire preferred rewards categories`               IS EMPTY
    `yuu account linked to the card`                       IS FALSE
    `HSBC Everyday Global Account deposits ADB this month` IS 50_000
    `PAssion membership registered and card linked in yuu` IS FALSE

-- uob-ladys-faq Q7 contrasts a Solitaire cardmember who elected two
-- categories with one who elected only one, and Q10 with one who elected
-- none. Three cardholders, one per answer.
GIVETH A Cardholder
`a Solitaire cardmember electing Dining and Family` MEANS Cardholder WITH
    `Solitaire preferred rewards categories`               IS LIST Dining, Family
    `yuu account linked to the card`                       IS FALSE
    `HSBC Everyday Global Account deposits ADB this month` IS 0
    `PAssion membership registered and card linked in yuu` IS FALSE

GIVETH A Cardholder
`a Solitaire cardmember electing Dining only` MEANS Cardholder WITH
    `Solitaire preferred rewards categories`               IS LIST Dining
    `yuu account linked to the card`                       IS FALSE
    `HSBC Everyday Global Account deposits ADB this month` IS 0
    `PAssion membership registered and card linked in yuu` IS FALSE

GIVETH A Cardholder
`a Solitaire cardmember who elected nothing` MEANS Cardholder WITH
    `Solitaire preferred rewards categories`               IS EMPTY
    `yuu account linked to the card`                       IS FALSE
    `HSBC Everyday Global Account deposits ADB this month` IS 0
    `PAssion membership registered and card linked in yuu` IS FALSE

-- dbs-yuu-card-tnc cl.11: points go to the yuu Account "which has been linked
-- to the DBS yuu principal cardmember at the point of transaction".
GIVETH A Cardholder
`a yuu cardmember with the card linked` MEANS Cardholder WITH
    `Solitaire preferred rewards categories`               IS EMPTY
    `yuu account linked to the card`                       IS TRUE
    `HSBC Everyday Global Account deposits ADB this month` IS 0
    `PAssion membership registered and card linked in yuu` IS FALSE

-- posb-passion-yuu-tnc cl.1: the Promotion is only for a Cardmember with a
-- PAssion membership, a yuu Account, and the PAssion Card linked in the yuu
-- App.
GIVETH A Cardholder
`a PAssion cardmember, registered and linked` MEANS Cardholder WITH
    `Solitaire preferred rewards categories`               IS EMPTY
    `yuu account linked to the card`                       IS TRUE
    `HSBC Everyday Global Account deposits ADB this month` IS 0
    `PAssion membership registered and card linked in yuu` IS TRUE

-- dbs-womans-card-tnc conditions nothing on a standing fact either.
GIVETH A Cardholder
`a DBS Woman's World cardmember` MEANS Cardholder WITH
    `Solitaire preferred rewards categories`               IS EMPTY
    `yuu account linked to the card`                       IS FALSE
    `HSBC Everyday Global Account deposits ADB this month` IS 0
    `PAssion membership registered and card linked in yuu` IS FALSE


§§ `Where the month stands`

-- The neutral month. Every card whose rate turns on no monthly threshold is
-- asserted against this one.
GIVETH A `Month position`
`a month with nothing spent yet` MEANS `Month position` WITH
    `yuu eligible spend so far this calendar month`                     IS 0
    `yuu participating merchants transacted so far this calendar month` IS 0
    `PAssion spend at Participating Stores so far this month`           IS 0
    `PAssion spend at non-Participating Stores so far this month`       IS 0

-- dbs-yuu-card-tnc cl.7(b): "i. Minimum S$800 worth of Eligible Spend charged
-- and posted to your Card, and ii. Transact at 4 Participating Merchants."
GIVETH A `Month position`
`a month meeting the yuu Minimum Spend Requirement` MEANS `Month position` WITH
    `yuu eligible spend so far this calendar month`                     IS 900
    `yuu participating merchants transacted so far this calendar month` IS 4
    `PAssion spend at Participating Stores so far this month`           IS 0
    `PAssion spend at non-Participating Stores so far this month`       IS 0

-- posb-passion-yuu-tnc cl.8(a): "i. At least S$300 total spend at
-- Participating Stores ii. At least S$400 total spend at non-Participating
-- Stores".
GIVETH A `Month position`
`a month meeting both PAssion thresholds` MEANS `Month position` WITH
    `yuu eligible spend so far this calendar month`                     IS 0
    `yuu participating merchants transacted so far this calendar month` IS 0
    `PAssion spend at Participating Stores so far this month`           IS 350
    `PAssion spend at non-Participating Stores so far this month`       IS 450


§§ `Citi Rewards`

-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
-- citi-rewards-10x-tnc cl.13, "Illustration", row #1, verbatim:
--
--   Transaction | Transaction Category | Points Eligible Transaction |
--   Transaction Amount | Base Points Earned | Bonus Points Earned
--   #1 | Department Stores | 10X | S$800.99 | 800 * 1 = 800 | 800 * 9 = 7,200
--
-- The illustration gives a TOTAL, not a rate. 800 Base + 7,200 Bonus = 8,000
-- Points on a charge the same clause rounds down to S$800, so the rate it
-- implies is 8,000 / 800 = 10 Points per S$1 -- which is cl.13(i)'s 1 Base
-- Point plus cl.13(ii)'s 9 Bonus Points. That per-dollar figure is what is
-- asserted; the rounding-down of S$800.99 to S$800 is an allocation question
-- the domain does not carry (miles-card-domain.l4, "Where the month stands").
--
-- MCC 5311 (Department Stores) is the first row of cl.6(i)'s table, so the
-- 10X limb fires on the code alone and the answer does not turn on the
-- merchant indicator. The illustration does not say whether the charge was
-- made in the store or on its website, so the indicator is Unknown.
-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
GIVETH A Transaction
`Citi illustration #1 -- S$800.99 at a department store` MEANS Transaction WITH
    `merchant name`                IS "A department store"
    `merchant`                     IS `Another merchant`
    `merchant category code`       IS 5311
    `transaction description`      IS "DEPARTMENT STORE"
    `description patterns`         IS EMPTY
    `charge kind`                  IS `Retail purchase`
    `amount`                       IS 800.99
    `currency`                     IS "SGD"
    `posted in a foreign currency` IS FALSE
    `transaction date`             IS YMD 2026 9 10
    `posting date`                 IS YMD 2026 9 11
    `payment channel`              IS `Inserted or swiped at a terminal`
    `credential`                   IS `The physical card`
    `merchant indicator`           IS Unknown
    `made in Singapore`            IS TRUE

#ASSERT (`the rate on` `Citi Rewards` `a Citi Rewards cardholder` `a month with nothing spent yet` `Citi illustration #1 -- S$800.99 at a department store`)'s `points per dollar` EQUALS 10
#ASSERT (`the rate on` `Citi Rewards` `a Citi Rewards cardholder` `a month with nothing spent yet` `Citi illustration #1 -- S$800.99 at a department store`)'s `earns the bonus rate` EQUALS TRUE

-- cl.13, third paragraph: "Base Points are not subject to any cap. However,
-- Bonus Points are subject to a cap of 9,000 Bonus Points per statement
-- month." At cl.13(ii)'s 9 Bonus Points per S$1 that is S$1,000 of
-- bonus-earning spend, and the basis Citi names is the STATEMENT month, not
-- the calendar month -- the one place in this corpus where the two differ.
#ASSERT (`the rate on` `Citi Rewards` `a Citi Rewards cardholder` `a month with nothing spent yet` `Citi illustration #1 -- S$800.99 at a department store`)'s cap's capped EQUALS TRUE
#ASSERT (`the rate on` `Citi Rewards` `a Citi Rewards cardholder` `a month with nothing spent yet` `Citi illustration #1 -- S$800.99 at a department store`)'s cap's `bonus spend per month` EQUALS 1000
#ASSERT (`the rate on` `Citi Rewards` `a Citi Rewards cardholder` `a month with nothing spent yet` `Citi illustration #1 -- S$800.99 at a department store`)'s cap's basis EQUALS `Statement month`

-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
-- citi-rewards-10x-tnc cl.13, "Illustration", row #2, verbatim:
--
--   #2 | Shoe Stores | 10X | S$550.24 | 550 * 1 = 550 | 550 * 9 = 4,950
--
-- 550 + 4,950 = 5,500 Points on S$550 rounded down, so 5,500 / 550 = 10
-- Points per S$1 again. MCC 5661 (Shoe Stores) is in cl.6(i)'s table.
--
-- The illustration's Total row and its footnote -- "^As Bonus Points are
-- capped at 9,000 Bonus Points per statement month, Eligible Cardholder will
-- only be awarded a maximum of 9,000 Bonus Points even though Bonus Points
-- for both transactions amounts to a total of 12,150" -- is the ALLOCATION
-- of one month's cap across two charges, which is out of scope for this
-- corpus (spec section 6). The cap FIGURE is asserted above; the running
-- total is not expressible.
-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
GIVETH A Transaction
`Citi illustration #2 -- S$550.24 at a shoe store` MEANS Transaction WITH
    `merchant name`                IS "A shoe store"
    `merchant`                     IS `Another merchant`
    `merchant category code`       IS 5661
    `transaction description`      IS "SHOE STORE"
    `description patterns`         IS EMPTY
    `charge kind`                  IS `Retail purchase`
    `amount`                       IS 550.24
    `currency`                     IS "SGD"
    `posted in a foreign currency` IS FALSE
    `transaction date`             IS YMD 2026 9 10
    `posting date`                 IS YMD 2026 9 11
    `payment channel`              IS `Inserted or swiped at a terminal`
    `credential`                   IS `The physical card`
    `merchant indicator`           IS Unknown
    `made in Singapore`            IS TRUE

#ASSERT (`the rate on` `Citi Rewards` `a Citi Rewards cardholder` `a month with nothing spent yet` `Citi illustration #2 -- S$550.24 at a shoe store`)'s `points per dollar` EQUALS 10
#ASSERT (`the rate on` `Citi Rewards` `a Citi Rewards cardholder` `a month with nothing spent yet` `Citi illustration #2 -- S$550.24 at a shoe store`)'s `earns the bonus rate` EQUALS TRUE

-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
-- citi-rewards-10x-faq Q1, answer (ii), verbatim: "a Qualifying Charge made
-- at any online retail merchants, excluding mobile wallet and travel-related
-- transactions*".
--
-- The T&C's matching limb, cl.6(ii), says what "online" means: "These refer
-- to Qualifying Charges made via the internet or mobile applications, which
-- is determined by system indicators reflecting that it is an online
-- transaction ... These indicators are decided by the relevant merchant
-- and/or their acquirer and are not determined by Citibank."
--
-- So this example DOES state the channel outcome, and the fixture carries
-- `Flags online` rather than Unknown. MCC 5732 (Electronics Sales) is in NO
-- cl.6(i) list, so the 10X here is earned by the online limb alone -- which
-- is what makes this case worth having beside the two MCC cases above.
--
-- The credential is the physical card on file, NOT a wallet token: the FAQ
-- excludes "mobile wallet" from this limb.
--
-- citi-rewards-10x-faq Q4 restates the same rate and the same cap as cl.13:
-- "1 Base Point for every S$1 ... 9 Bonus Points for every S$1 ... Bonus
-- Points are subject to a cap of 9,000 Bonus Points per statement month."
-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
GIVETH A Transaction
`Citi FAQ Q1(ii) -- an online retail merchant` MEANS Transaction WITH
    `merchant name`                IS "An online electronics retailer"
    `merchant`                     IS `Another merchant`
    `merchant category code`       IS 5732
    `transaction description`      IS "ONLINE ELECTRONICS"
    `description patterns`         IS EMPTY
    `charge kind`                  IS `Retail purchase`
    `amount`                       IS 200
    `currency`                     IS "SGD"
    `posted in a foreign currency` IS FALSE
    `transaction date`             IS YMD 2026 9 10
    `posting date`                 IS YMD 2026 9 11
    `payment channel`              IS `Paid in a website or app`
    `credential`                   IS `The physical card`
    `merchant indicator`           IS `Flags online`
    `made in Singapore`            IS TRUE

#ASSERT (`the rate on` `Citi Rewards` `a Citi Rewards cardholder` `a month with nothing spent yet` `Citi FAQ Q1(ii) -- an online retail merchant`)'s `points per dollar` EQUALS 10
#ASSERT (`the rate on` `Citi Rewards` `a Citi Rewards cardholder` `a month with nothing spent yet` `Citi FAQ Q1(ii) -- an online retail merchant`)'s `earns the bonus rate` EQUALS TRUE
#ASSERT (`the rate on` `Citi Rewards` `a Citi Rewards cardholder` `a month with nothing spent yet` `Citi FAQ Q1(ii) -- an online retail merchant`)'s cap's `bonus spend per month` EQUALS 1000
#ASSERT (`the rate on` `Citi Rewards` `a Citi Rewards cardholder` `a month with nothing spent yet` `Citi FAQ Q1(ii) -- an online retail merchant`)'s cap's basis EQUALS `Statement month`


§§ `HSBC Revolution`

-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
-- hsbc-revolution-reward-points-tnc cl.9, verbatim: "For avoidance of doubt,
-- the maximum total Reward points that may be awarded for every SGD1 of an
-- Eligible Transaction is 20 Reward points, as illustrated below:"
--
--   | Base Points earned | Bonus Points earned | Total Reward points earned | Bonus Points Cap
--   Cardholders with Deposits ADB of >=SGD50,000 for the calendar month in
--   which the Eligible Transaction was posted
--                        | 1 Reward point | 19 Reward points | 20 Reward points
--                        | Subject to a cap of 22,800 Bonus Points per calendar month
--   All other Cardholders
--                        | 1 Reward point |  9 Reward points | 10 Reward points
--                        | Subject to a cap of  9,000 Bonus Points per calendar month
--
-- The cl.9 table states the rate per SGD1 directly, so no division is needed
-- for the rate. The caps are stated in POINTS and the domain carries dollars:
-- 22,800 / 19 = S$1,200 and 9,000 / 9 = S$1,000 of bonus-earning spend, on
-- the CALENDAR month basis cl.7.2 names.
--
-- The transaction is an online charge at MCC 5812 (Eating Places and
-- Restaurants), row 46 of cl.7's table, so it is an Eligible Transaction by
-- the cl.6 "Selected Online Transactions" limb. cl.6 defines that limb by the
-- acquirer's indicator -- "HSBC determines whether a transaction is a
-- Selected Online Transaction based on system indicators which are determined
-- by the merchants and the merchant's acquiring bank" -- so the fixture
-- states `Flags online`.
-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
GIVETH A Transaction
`HSBC cl.9 -- an online dining charge` MEANS Transaction WITH
    `merchant name`                IS "A restaurant's website"
    `merchant`                     IS `Another merchant`
    `merchant category code`       IS 5812
    `transaction description`      IS "RESTAURANT ONLINE"
    `description patterns`         IS EMPTY
    `charge kind`                  IS `Retail purchase`
    `amount`                       IS 100
    `currency`                     IS "SGD"
    `posted in a foreign currency` IS FALSE
    `transaction date`             IS YMD 2026 9 10
    `posting date`                 IS YMD 2026 9 11
    `payment channel`              IS `Paid in a website or app`
    `credential`                   IS `The physical card`
    `merchant indicator`           IS `Flags online`
    `made in Singapore`            IS TRUE

-- Row 2 of the cl.9 table: "All other Cardholders ... 10 Reward points".
#ASSERT (`the rate on` `HSBC Revolution` `an HSBC cardholder below the deposits tier` `a month with nothing spent yet` `HSBC cl.9 -- an online dining charge`)'s `points per dollar` EQUALS 10
#ASSERT (`the rate on` `HSBC Revolution` `an HSBC cardholder below the deposits tier` `a month with nothing spent yet` `HSBC cl.9 -- an online dining charge`)'s `earns the bonus rate` EQUALS TRUE
#ASSERT (`the rate on` `HSBC Revolution` `an HSBC cardholder below the deposits tier` `a month with nothing spent yet` `HSBC cl.9 -- an online dining charge`)'s cap's capped EQUALS TRUE
#ASSERT (`the rate on` `HSBC Revolution` `an HSBC cardholder below the deposits tier` `a month with nothing spent yet` `HSBC cl.9 -- an online dining charge`)'s cap's `bonus spend per month` EQUALS 1000
#ASSERT (`the rate on` `HSBC Revolution` `an HSBC cardholder below the deposits tier` `a month with nothing spent yet` `HSBC cl.9 -- an online dining charge`)'s cap's basis EQUALS `Calendar month`

-- Row 1 of the cl.9 table: the same charge, the same month, the same card --
-- only the Deposits ADB changes, and the rate doubles.
#ASSERT (`the rate on` `HSBC Revolution` `an HSBC cardholder at the deposits tier` `a month with nothing spent yet` `HSBC cl.9 -- an online dining charge`)'s `points per dollar` EQUALS 20
#ASSERT (`the rate on` `HSBC Revolution` `an HSBC cardholder at the deposits tier` `a month with nothing spent yet` `HSBC cl.9 -- an online dining charge`)'s `earns the bonus rate` EQUALS TRUE
#ASSERT (`the rate on` `HSBC Revolution` `an HSBC cardholder at the deposits tier` `a month with nothing spent yet` `HSBC cl.9 -- an online dining charge`)'s cap's `bonus spend per month` EQUALS 1200
#ASSERT (`the rate on` `HSBC Revolution` `an HSBC cardholder at the deposits tier` `a month with nothing spent yet` `HSBC cl.9 -- an online dining charge`)'s cap's basis EQUALS `Calendar month`

-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
-- hsbc-revolution-faq Q3, verbatim: "For example, a SGD20 online transaction
-- is posted on 27 February. Base Points (1X) of 20 Reward Points will
-- credited by your next statement cycle while the Bonus Points of 180 Reward
-- Points (9X) will be credited by 31 March."
--
-- A TOTAL, not a rate: 20 + 180 = 200 Reward points on SGD20, so 200 / 20 =
-- 10 Reward points per SGD1, which is the cl.9 table's second row.
--
-- The FAQ does not say which merchant, so the MCC is supplied from cl.7's
-- table (5812, Eating Places and Restaurants) -- the example is about the
-- arithmetic and the crediting dates, and it only makes sense for a
-- transaction that is Eligible under cl.7. The two dates are the FAQ's own.
-- The crediting SCHEDULE the example is really about (cl.10: Base Points on
-- the statement cycle, Bonus Points by the last day of the following calendar
-- month) is not expressible: `Rate answer` carries a rate, not a payout date.
-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
GIVETH A Transaction
`HSBC FAQ Q3 -- SGD20 online, posted 27 February` MEANS Transaction WITH
    `merchant name`                IS "An online merchant"
    `merchant`                     IS `Another merchant`
    `merchant category code`       IS 5812
    `transaction description`      IS "ONLINE MERCHANT"
    `description patterns`         IS EMPTY
    `charge kind`                  IS `Retail purchase`
    `amount`                       IS 20
    `currency`                     IS "SGD"
    `posted in a foreign currency` IS FALSE
    `transaction date`             IS YMD 2026 2 26
    `posting date`                 IS YMD 2026 2 27
    `payment channel`              IS `Paid in a website or app`
    `credential`                   IS `The physical card`
    `merchant indicator`           IS `Flags online`
    `made in Singapore`            IS TRUE

#ASSERT (`the rate on` `HSBC Revolution` `an HSBC cardholder below the deposits tier` `a month with nothing spent yet` `HSBC FAQ Q3 -- SGD20 online, posted 27 February`)'s `points per dollar` EQUALS 10
#ASSERT (`the rate on` `HSBC Revolution` `an HSBC cardholder below the deposits tier` `a month with nothing spent yet` `HSBC FAQ Q3 -- SGD20 online, posted 27 February`)'s `earns the bonus rate` EQUALS TRUE

-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
-- hsbc-revolution-faq Q1, verbatim: "Online purchases refer to all posted
-- qualified retail transactions made via the internet, either done locally or
-- abroad, for the purchase of goods or services provided by any merchants.
-- This includes credential-on-file payments that require you to store your
-- credit card information with a merchant or payment facilitator to make
-- future purchases."
--
-- cl.6 says the same thing in the T&C: "including credential-on-file payments
-- when the Cardholder stores the Card information with a merchant or payment
-- facilitator to make future purchases." FAQ and T&C agree here, which is
-- worth an assertion precisely because the next section shows two places
-- where they do not.
--
-- MCC 5968 (Direct Marketing -- Continuity/Subscription Merchants) is row 38
-- of cl.7's table: a recurring subscription billed to a card on file.
-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
GIVETH A Transaction
`HSBC FAQ Q1 -- a credential-on-file subscription` MEANS Transaction WITH
    `merchant name`                IS "A subscription service"
    `merchant`                     IS `Another merchant`
    `merchant category code`       IS 5968
    `transaction description`      IS "SUBSCRIPTION"
    `description patterns`         IS EMPTY
    `charge kind`                  IS `Retail purchase`
    `amount`                       IS 30
    `currency`                     IS "SGD"
    `posted in a foreign currency` IS FALSE
    `transaction date`             IS YMD 2026 9 10
    `posting date`                 IS YMD 2026 9 11
    `payment channel`              IS `Card on file or recurring billing`
    `credential`                   IS `The physical card`
    `merchant indicator`           IS `Flags online`
    `made in Singapore`            IS TRUE

#ASSERT (`the rate on` `HSBC Revolution` `an HSBC cardholder below the deposits tier` `a month with nothing spent yet` `HSBC FAQ Q1 -- a credential-on-file subscription`)'s `points per dollar` EQUALS 10
#ASSERT (`the rate on` `HSBC Revolution` `an HSBC cardholder below the deposits tier` `a month with nothing spent yet` `HSBC FAQ Q1 -- a credential-on-file subscription`)'s `earns the bonus rate` EQUALS TRUE

-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
-- hsbc-revolution-faq Q4, verbatim: "Why did I not earn Reward Points on my
-- purchase? The purchase you made is likely an excluded transaction which
-- will not earn you any Reward points. Such transactions include donations,
-- quasi-cash transactions (i.e. cryptocurrency transactions), payments to
-- education institution, cleaning, maintenance and janitorial services or
-- insurance companies."
--
-- The T&C agrees twice over: cl.4 excludes "Payments to educational
-- institutions" from Qualifying Transactions, and cl.4.2 lists MCC 8220
-- (Colleges, Universities, Professional Schools, and Junior Colleges) at row
-- 32 of the excluded-MCC table. So the answer is NO points at all -- not the
-- cl.8 fallback of 1 Reward point, which applies only to Qualifying
-- Transactions that are not Eligible Transactions.
-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
GIVETH A Transaction
`HSBC FAQ Q4 -- a university fee payment` MEANS Transaction WITH
    `merchant name`                IS "A university"
    `merchant`                     IS `Another merchant`
    `merchant category code`       IS 8220
    `transaction description`      IS "UNIVERSITY FEES"
    `description patterns`         IS EMPTY
    `charge kind`                  IS `Retail purchase`
    `amount`                       IS 4_000
    `currency`                     IS "SGD"
    `posted in a foreign currency` IS FALSE
    `transaction date`             IS YMD 2026 9 10
    `posting date`                 IS YMD 2026 9 11
    `payment channel`              IS `Paid in a website or app`
    `credential`                   IS `The physical card`
    `merchant indicator`           IS `Flags online`
    `made in Singapore`            IS TRUE

#ASSERT (`the rate on` `HSBC Revolution` `an HSBC cardholder below the deposits tier` `a month with nothing spent yet` `HSBC FAQ Q4 -- a university fee payment`)'s `points per dollar` EQUALS 0
#ASSERT (`the rate on` `HSBC Revolution` `an HSBC cardholder below the deposits tier` `a month with nothing spent yet` `HSBC FAQ Q4 -- a university fee payment`)'s `earns the bonus rate` EQUALS FALSE


§§ `DBS yuu`

-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
-- dbs-yuu-card-tnc cl.6, verbatim: "The mechanics of the Base Rewards are as
-- illustrated in the table below. For every S$1 spent at the following Spend
-- Categories that is charged and posted to your DBS yuu Card, you will earn
-- the respective Base Rewards.
--
--   Spend Categories        | Base Rewards
--   yuu Merchant Spend      | 1 yuu Point (0.5% cash rebates)
--   SimplyGo                | 0.5 yuu Point (0.25% cash rebates)
--   Non-yuu Merchant Spend  | 0.5 yuu Point (0.25% cash rebates)"
--
-- and cl.7(a), verbatim: "No minimum spend required to earn the following
-- Bonus Rewards. ... Spend Categories | Bonus Rewards / yuu Merchant Spend |
-- 9 yuu Points (4.5% cash rebates) / SimplyGo | 9.5 yuu Points (4.75% cash
-- rebates)".
--
-- With the Minimum Spend Requirement NOT met, a yuu Merchant charge therefore
-- earns 1 + 9 = 10 yuu Points per S$1, and a SimplyGo ride 0.5 + 9.5 = 10.
-- The two categories landing on the same figure is the document's own
-- arithmetic, not ours, and is the check that the tables are read as adding.
--
-- cl.12 states the conversion in a held document -- "1 yuu Point is
-- equivalent to 0.5% cash rebate or 0.28 miles or more" -- so miles are
-- assertable here, unlike on the HSBC and Citi cards.
--
-- READ "OR MORE" AS A FLOOR, NOT AN EQUALITY. cl.12 does not say a yuu Point
-- is worth 0.28 miles; it says 0.28 OR MORE, "depending on the redemption
-- item on the yuu Rewards catalogue". So the assertions below are AT LEAST,
-- which is the sentence the clause actually contains, and 10 x 0.28 = 2.8 is
-- the floor on the miles this charge earns rather than the figure.
--
-- THESE FOUR ASSERTIONS ONCE FAILED, AND THE FAILURE WAS THEIR WHOLE POINT.
-- cl.7 prices the monthly cap twice inside one parenthesis -- "capped at
-- 28,800 yuu Points (worth up to S$144 cash rebates or 8,000 miles) per
-- calendar month" -- and 8,000 / 28,800 = 0.2777... miles per yuu Point. The
-- first-pass encoding took that ratio as the conversion, reasoning that it
-- sat just below cl.12's 0.28 and was therefore consistent with "or more".
-- That reads the inequality backwards: a value BELOW a floor does not satisfy
-- the floor, it breaches it. Because these assertions were written to state
-- cl.12's own sentence rather than to adopt whatever figure the module
-- happened to carry, all four failed, and the gap between the two clauses
-- surfaced instead of being absorbed into an encoding decision nobody saw.
--
-- RULED FOR cl.12 BY THE CONDUCTOR ON 2026-09-21, reversing that first pass.
-- The fork is recorded as `F-yuu-conversion-floor` in
-- source/fork-register.json, which keeps the rejected reading beside the
-- taken one. The argument that settled it is inside cl.7's own parenthesis:
-- its cash limb is EXACT, because 28,800 at 0.5% is S$144 to the cent, while
-- its mile limb is not, because 28,800 at 0.28 is 8,064 and the clause prints
-- 8,000. One limb rounded and the other exact is what tells a rounded
-- illustration apart from a stated equivalence -- and cl.12 is in any case
-- the clause whose subject IS the conversion, where cl.7's subject is the
-- cap. `miles per yuu Point` in dbs-yuu.l4 is now 0.28, and all four
-- assertions below hold.
--
-- THEY ARE KEPT AS WITNESSES, NOT AS TESTS THAT HAPPEN TO PASS. The fork
-- register names them in exactly that capacity: they are the four places
-- where a return to cl.7's ratio would show itself, and each would fail again
-- the moment anyone reinstated it.
--
-- LEAVE THEM SPELLED "AT LEAST". An EQUALS here would assert an equality
-- cl.12 does not state, and it would also begin failing if a redemption item
-- ever made the conversion richer than its floor -- which is the one thing
-- cl.12 expressly contemplates.
--
-- cl.6(i): "There is no minimum spend required, and no cap to the Base
-- Rewards." cl.7: "Total Bonus Rewards is capped at 28,800 yuu Points (worth
-- up to S$144 cash rebates or 8,000 miles) per calendar month." The cap is
-- stated in POINTS against a rate that itself changes with the threshold, so
-- the dollars of bonus-earning spend it admits is not a figure the document
-- gives; only the basis and the fact of a cap are asserted.
--
-- cl.10: "Eligible Spend must be charged to your DBS yuu Card within the
-- calendar month, based on transaction date."
-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
GIVETH A Transaction
`yuu cl.6 -- S$100 of groceries at Cold Storage` MEANS Transaction WITH
    `merchant name`                IS "Cold Storage"
    `merchant`                     IS `Cold Storage`
    `merchant category code`       IS 5411
    `transaction description`      IS "COLD STORAGE"
    `description patterns`         IS EMPTY
    `charge kind`                  IS `Retail purchase`
    `amount`                       IS 100
    `currency`                     IS "SGD"
    `posted in a foreign currency` IS FALSE
    `transaction date`             IS YMD 2026 9 10
    `posting date`                 IS YMD 2026 9 11
    `payment channel`              IS `Tapped at a terminal`
    `credential`                   IS `The physical card`
    `merchant indicator`           IS Unknown
    `made in Singapore`            IS TRUE

#ASSERT (`the rate on` `DBS yuu Visa` `a yuu cardmember with the card linked` `a month with nothing spent yet` `yuu cl.6 -- S$100 of groceries at Cold Storage`)'s `points per dollar` EQUALS 10
#ASSERT (`the rate on` `DBS yuu Visa` `a yuu cardmember with the card linked` `a month with nothing spent yet` `yuu cl.6 -- S$100 of groceries at Cold Storage`)'s `earns the bonus rate` EQUALS TRUE
#ASSERT (`the rate on` `DBS yuu Visa` `a yuu cardmember with the card linked` `a month with nothing spent yet` `yuu cl.6 -- S$100 of groceries at Cold Storage`)'s `miles per point` AT LEAST 0.28
#ASSERT (`the rate on` `DBS yuu Visa` `a yuu cardmember with the card linked` `a month with nothing spent yet` `yuu cl.6 -- S$100 of groceries at Cold Storage`)'s `conversion status` EQUALS Verified
#ASSERT (`the rate on` `DBS yuu Visa` `a yuu cardmember with the card linked` `a month with nothing spent yet` `yuu cl.6 -- S$100 of groceries at Cold Storage`)'s `miles per dollar` AT LEAST 2.8
#ASSERT (`the rate on` `DBS yuu Visa` `a yuu cardmember with the card linked` `a month with nothing spent yet` `yuu cl.6 -- S$100 of groceries at Cold Storage`)'s cap's capped EQUALS TRUE
#ASSERT (`the rate on` `DBS yuu Visa` `a yuu cardmember with the card linked` `a month with nothing spent yet` `yuu cl.6 -- S$100 of groceries at Cold Storage`)'s cap's basis EQUALS `Calendar month`
#ASSERT (`the rate on` `DBS yuu Visa` `a yuu cardmember with the card linked` `a month with nothing spent yet` `yuu cl.6 -- S$100 of groceries at Cold Storage`)'s cap's attribution EQUALS `By transaction date`

-- cl.8's Participating Merchants table, verbatim: "SimplyGo | Bus and train
-- rides via SimplyGo". cl.6 gives SimplyGo a base of 0.5 and cl.7(a) a bonus
-- of 9.5, so 10 yuu Points per S$1 -- the same figure the Cold Storage case
-- reaches from 1 + 9.
GIVETH A Transaction
`yuu cl.6 -- a SimplyGo bus ride` MEANS Transaction WITH
    `merchant name`                IS "SimplyGo"
    `merchant`                     IS SimplyGo
    `merchant category code`       IS 4111
    `transaction description`      IS "SIMPLYGO"
    `description patterns`         IS EMPTY
    `charge kind`                  IS `Retail purchase`
    `amount`                       IS 2.20
    `currency`                     IS "SGD"
    `posted in a foreign currency` IS FALSE
    `transaction date`             IS YMD 2026 9 10
    `posting date`                 IS YMD 2026 9 11
    `payment channel`              IS `Tapped at a terminal`
    `credential`                   IS `The physical card`
    `merchant indicator`           IS Unknown
    `made in Singapore`            IS TRUE

#ASSERT (`the rate on` `DBS yuu Visa` `a yuu cardmember with the card linked` `a month with nothing spent yet` `yuu cl.6 -- a SimplyGo bus ride`)'s `points per dollar` EQUALS 10
#ASSERT (`the rate on` `DBS yuu Visa` `a yuu cardmember with the card linked` `a month with nothing spent yet` `yuu cl.6 -- a SimplyGo bus ride`)'s `earns the bonus rate` EQUALS TRUE

-- cl.6's third row, verbatim: "Non-yuu Merchant Spend | 0.5 yuu Point (0.25%
-- cash rebates)". cl.7(a) and cl.7(b) list only yuu Merchant Spend and
-- SimplyGo, so a non-yuu merchant earns the base and nothing else, at any
-- point in the month. 0.5 x 0.28 = 0.14 miles per S$1, stated as a FLOOR for
-- the reason set out under the Cold Storage case above, and one of the four
-- witnesses to `F-yuu-conversion-floor`.
GIVETH A Transaction
`yuu cl.6 -- S$100 at a non-yuu merchant` MEANS Transaction WITH
    `merchant name`                IS "A restaurant"
    `merchant`                     IS `Another merchant`
    `merchant category code`       IS 5812
    `transaction description`      IS "RESTAURANT"
    `description patterns`         IS EMPTY
    `charge kind`                  IS `Retail purchase`
    `amount`                       IS 100
    `currency`                     IS "SGD"
    `posted in a foreign currency` IS FALSE
    `transaction date`             IS YMD 2026 9 10
    `posting date`                 IS YMD 2026 9 11
    `payment channel`              IS `Inserted or swiped at a terminal`
    `credential`                   IS `The physical card`
    `merchant indicator`           IS Unknown
    `made in Singapore`            IS TRUE

#ASSERT (`the rate on` `DBS yuu Visa` `a yuu cardmember with the card linked` `a month with nothing spent yet` `yuu cl.6 -- S$100 at a non-yuu merchant`)'s `points per dollar` EQUALS 0.5
#ASSERT (`the rate on` `DBS yuu Visa` `a yuu cardmember with the card linked` `a month with nothing spent yet` `yuu cl.6 -- S$100 at a non-yuu merchant`)'s `earns the bonus rate` EQUALS FALSE
#ASSERT (`the rate on` `DBS yuu Visa` `a yuu cardmember with the card linked` `a month with nothing spent yet` `yuu cl.6 -- S$100 at a non-yuu merchant`)'s `miles per dollar` AT LEAST 0.14

-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
-- dbs-yuu-card-tnc cl.7(b), verbatim: "To earn the following Bonus Rewards,
-- Cardmembers must meet these spend requirements each calendar month
-- ('Minimum Spend Requirement'): i. Minimum S$800 worth of Eligible Spend
-- charged and posted to your Card, and ii. Transact at 4 Participating
-- Merchants.
--
--   Spend Categories    | Bonus Rewards
--   yuu Merchant Spend  | 26 yuu Points (13% cash rebates)
--   SimplyGo            | 26 yuu Points (13% cash rebates)"
--
-- READING NOTE, AND IT IS A REAL AMBIGUITY IN THE SOURCE. cl.7 opens "Total
-- Bonus Rewards is capped at 28,800 yuu Points", and prints tables (a) and
-- (b) as two tables of Bonus Rewards, not as a table and its replacement. On
-- the ADDING reading a yuu Merchant charge earns 1 + 9 + 26 = 36 yuu Points
-- per S$1 and a SimplyGo ride 0.5 + 9.5 + 26 = 36 -- the same figure from two
-- different starting points, which is unlikely to be a coincidence, and 36 x
-- 0.5% = 18% cash rebates, the headline the sibling PAssion document names in
-- its own title ("Up to 9% Cash Rebates (18X yuu Points)"). On the REPLACING
-- reading they are 27 and 26.5, which agree with nothing.
--
-- The assertions take the adding reading. If they fail at 27, the encoding
-- has taken the other one, and that is the finding -- do not change these
-- numbers to match. 36 x 0.28 = 10.08 miles per S$1, again as cl.12's floor
-- and again a witness to `F-yuu-conversion-floor`. Note that 10.08 is round
-- in nothing. Under the rejected ratio 36 points came to exactly 10.0 miles
-- per dollar, and dbs-yuu.l4's first pass offered that roundness as a second
-- argument for reading cl.7's tables as adding; the fork register records
-- that support as withdrawn. It was an artefact of the conversion that was
-- rejected, and it corroborates nothing now. The additive reading stands on
-- the two arguments given above, neither of which touches miles at all.
-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
#ASSERT (`the rate on` `DBS yuu Visa` `a yuu cardmember with the card linked` `a month meeting the yuu Minimum Spend Requirement` `yuu cl.6 -- S$100 of groceries at Cold Storage`)'s `points per dollar` EQUALS 36
#ASSERT (`the rate on` `DBS yuu Visa` `a yuu cardmember with the card linked` `a month meeting the yuu Minimum Spend Requirement` `yuu cl.6 -- S$100 of groceries at Cold Storage`)'s `earns the bonus rate` EQUALS TRUE
#ASSERT (`the rate on` `DBS yuu Visa` `a yuu cardmember with the card linked` `a month meeting the yuu Minimum Spend Requirement` `yuu cl.6 -- S$100 of groceries at Cold Storage`)'s `miles per dollar` AT LEAST 10.08
#ASSERT (`the rate on` `DBS yuu Visa` `a yuu cardmember with the card linked` `a month meeting the yuu Minimum Spend Requirement` `yuu cl.6 -- a SimplyGo bus ride`)'s `points per dollar` EQUALS 36

-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
-- dbs-yuu-card-tnc Appendix 1, Cold Storage row, verbatim, under "Applicable
-- to Base and Bonus Rewards": "Bonus yuu Points will not be awarded for
-- transactions made at Cold Storage On The Go (within Esso Stations), only
-- base 0.5 yuu point (equivalent to 0.25% cash rebates) will be awarded.
-- Transactions will be eligible to count towards card's minimum spend
-- requirement."
--
-- The Appendix states the answer as a figure, so this is a worked example and
-- not merely an exclusion: 0.5 yuu Point per S$1, and 0.5 rather than cl.6's
-- 1 -- the Appendix drops it to the non-yuu-merchant base. It holds whether
-- or not the Minimum Spend Requirement is met, which is what the second
-- assertion checks.
-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
GIVETH A Transaction
`yuu Appendix 1 -- Cold Storage On The Go, within an Esso station` MEANS Transaction WITH
    `merchant name`                IS "Cold Storage On The Go"
    `merchant`                     IS `Cold Storage On The Go`
    `merchant category code`       IS 5541
    `transaction description`      IS "COLD STORAGE ON THE GO"
    `description patterns`         IS EMPTY
    `charge kind`                  IS `Retail purchase`
    `amount`                       IS 12
    `currency`                     IS "SGD"
    `posted in a foreign currency` IS FALSE
    `transaction date`             IS YMD 2026 9 10
    `posting date`                 IS YMD 2026 9 11
    `payment channel`              IS `Tapped at a terminal`
    `credential`                   IS `The physical card`
    `merchant indicator`           IS Unknown
    `made in Singapore`            IS TRUE

#ASSERT (`the rate on` `DBS yuu Visa` `a yuu cardmember with the card linked` `a month with nothing spent yet` `yuu Appendix 1 -- Cold Storage On The Go, within an Esso station`)'s `points per dollar` EQUALS 0.5
#ASSERT (`the rate on` `DBS yuu Visa` `a yuu cardmember with the card linked` `a month with nothing spent yet` `yuu Appendix 1 -- Cold Storage On The Go, within an Esso station`)'s `earns the bonus rate` EQUALS FALSE
#ASSERT (`the rate on` `DBS yuu Visa` `a yuu cardmember with the card linked` `a month meeting the yuu Minimum Spend Requirement` `yuu Appendix 1 -- Cold Storage On The Go, within an Esso station`)'s `points per dollar` EQUALS 0.5

-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
-- dbs-yuu-card-tnc Appendix 1, Charge+ row, verbatim: "Charge+ | Charge+
-- Singapore | Applicable to Bonus Rewards ... Points will not be awarded for
-- any transactions made with DBS yuu American Express Card."
--
-- The exclusion sits under the "Applicable to Bonus Rewards" heading, so it
-- takes away cl.7(a)'s 9 and leaves cl.6's yuu Merchant base of 1. The same
-- charge on the Visa keeps both: 1 + 9 = 10. This is the one example in the
-- corpus that turns on the NETWORK rather than on anything about the charge,
-- which is why the domain makes the network part of the card's identity.
-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
GIVETH A Transaction
`yuu Appendix 1 -- a Charge+ charging session` MEANS Transaction WITH
    `merchant name`                IS "Charge+ Singapore"
    `merchant`                     IS `Charge+`
    `merchant category code`       IS 5552
    `transaction description`      IS "CHARGE+ SG"
    `description patterns`         IS EMPTY
    `charge kind`                  IS `Retail purchase`
    `amount`                       IS 25
    `currency`                     IS "SGD"
    `posted in a foreign currency` IS FALSE
    `transaction date`             IS YMD 2026 9 10
    `posting date`                 IS YMD 2026 9 11
    `payment channel`              IS `Paid in a website or app`
    `credential`                   IS `The physical card`
    `merchant indicator`           IS Unknown
    `made in Singapore`            IS TRUE

#ASSERT (`the rate on` `DBS yuu Visa` `a yuu cardmember with the card linked` `a month with nothing spent yet` `yuu Appendix 1 -- a Charge+ charging session`)'s `points per dollar` EQUALS 10
#ASSERT (`the rate on` `DBS yuu Visa` `a yuu cardmember with the card linked` `a month with nothing spent yet` `yuu Appendix 1 -- a Charge+ charging session`)'s `earns the bonus rate` EQUALS TRUE
#ASSERT (`the rate on` `DBS yuu American Express` `a yuu cardmember with the card linked` `a month with nothing spent yet` `yuu Appendix 1 -- a Charge+ charging session`)'s `points per dollar` EQUALS 1
#ASSERT (`the rate on` `DBS yuu American Express` `a yuu cardmember with the card linked` `a month with nothing spent yet` `yuu Appendix 1 -- a Charge+ charging session`)'s `earns the bonus rate` EQUALS FALSE

-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
-- dbs-yuu-card-tnc Appendix 1, 7-Eleven row, verbatim, under "Applicable to
-- Bonus Rewards": "Points will not be awarded for any transactions made with
-- DBS yuu American Express Card. With effect from 13 Aug 2026, American
-- Express Cards will be accepted at all 7-Eleven outlets islandwide. DBS yuu
-- American Express Cardmembers can earn bonus rewards on 7-Eleven
-- transactions w.e.f. 13 Aug 2026".
--
-- A DATED example, and the only one in the corpus where the same card, the
-- same merchant and the same amount give two different answers one day apart.
-- The Appendix says the bonus arrives WITH EFFECT FROM 13 Aug 2026, so 13 Aug
-- itself is inside the new rule and 12 Aug is outside. cl.10 attributes by
-- transaction date, which is the date the boundary is drawn against.
-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
GIVETH A Transaction
`yuu Appendix 1 -- 7-Eleven on 12 August 2026` MEANS Transaction WITH
    `merchant name`                IS "7-Eleven"
    `merchant`                     IS `7-Eleven`
    `merchant category code`       IS 5499
    `transaction description`      IS "7-ELEVEN"
    `description patterns`         IS EMPTY
    `charge kind`                  IS `Retail purchase`
    `amount`                       IS 8
    `currency`                     IS "SGD"
    `posted in a foreign currency` IS FALSE
    `transaction date`             IS YMD 2026 8 12
    `posting date`                 IS YMD 2026 8 13
    `payment channel`              IS `Tapped at a terminal`
    `credential`                   IS `The physical card`
    `merchant indicator`           IS Unknown
    `made in Singapore`            IS TRUE

GIVETH A Transaction
`yuu Appendix 1 -- 7-Eleven on 13 August 2026` MEANS Transaction WITH
    `merchant name`                IS "7-Eleven"
    `merchant`                     IS `7-Eleven`
    `merchant category code`       IS 5499
    `transaction description`      IS "7-ELEVEN"
    `description patterns`         IS EMPTY
    `charge kind`                  IS `Retail purchase`
    `amount`                       IS 8
    `currency`                     IS "SGD"
    `posted in a foreign currency` IS FALSE
    `transaction date`             IS YMD 2026 8 13
    `posting date`                 IS YMD 2026 8 14
    `payment channel`              IS `Tapped at a terminal`
    `credential`                   IS `The physical card`
    `merchant indicator`           IS Unknown
    `made in Singapore`            IS TRUE

#ASSERT (`the rate on` `DBS yuu American Express` `a yuu cardmember with the card linked` `a month with nothing spent yet` `yuu Appendix 1 -- 7-Eleven on 12 August 2026`)'s `earns the bonus rate` EQUALS FALSE
#ASSERT (`the rate on` `DBS yuu American Express` `a yuu cardmember with the card linked` `a month with nothing spent yet` `yuu Appendix 1 -- 7-Eleven on 12 August 2026`)'s `points per dollar` EQUALS 1
#ASSERT (`the rate on` `DBS yuu American Express` `a yuu cardmember with the card linked` `a month with nothing spent yet` `yuu Appendix 1 -- 7-Eleven on 13 August 2026`)'s `earns the bonus rate` EQUALS TRUE
#ASSERT (`the rate on` `DBS yuu American Express` `a yuu cardmember with the card linked` `a month with nothing spent yet` `yuu Appendix 1 -- 7-Eleven on 13 August 2026`)'s `points per dollar` EQUALS 10
#ASSERT (`the rate on` `DBS yuu Visa` `a yuu cardmember with the card linked` `a month with nothing spent yet` `yuu Appendix 1 -- 7-Eleven on 12 August 2026`)'s `points per dollar` EQUALS 10


§§ `POSB PAssion Debit`

-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
-- posb-passion-yuu-tnc cl.10, verbatim: "All yuu Points are awarded up to 2
-- decimal places. Example: S$1.50 spend at yuu merchant = 4.50 yuu points
-- (based on 3X Base Points)."
--
-- A TOTAL: 4.50 / 1.50 = 3 yuu Points per S$1, which is cl.6's Base Points
-- row ("1.5% cash rebates (3X yuu Points)") and cl.7(a) ("Cardmember can earn
-- 3X yuu points on every S$1 Qualified Spend made at Participating Stores").
-- Cold Storage is a Participating Store under cl.5(i) ("DFI Retail Group
-- (DFG): 7-Eleven, Cold Storage, CS Fresh, Giant, Guardian").
--
-- cl.7(c): "There is no minimum spend required, and no cap to the Base Points
-- awarded" -- so this figure holds in a month that meets nothing.
--
-- The transaction is dated inside the Promotion Period, because cl.3 confines
-- the Promotion to "1 October 2023 to 30 September 2025" and an example
-- outside it is not an example of this document. The status assertion below
-- is the separate question of whether the DOCUMENT is still good, which the
-- domain answers `Source expired` by name.
-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
GIVETH A Transaction
`PAssion cl.10 -- S$1.50 at a Participating Store` MEANS Transaction WITH
    `merchant name`                IS "Cold Storage"
    `merchant`                     IS `Cold Storage`
    `merchant category code`       IS 5411
    `transaction description`      IS "COLD STORAGE"
    `description patterns`         IS EMPTY
    `charge kind`                  IS `Retail purchase`
    `amount`                       IS 1.50
    `currency`                     IS "SGD"
    `posted in a foreign currency` IS FALSE
    `transaction date`             IS YMD 2025 9 15
    `posting date`                 IS YMD 2025 9 16
    `payment channel`              IS `Tapped at a terminal`
    `credential`                   IS `The physical card`
    `merchant indicator`           IS Unknown
    `made in Singapore`            IS TRUE

#ASSERT (`the rate on` `POSB PAssion Debit` `a PAssion cardmember, registered and linked` `a month with nothing spent yet` `PAssion cl.10 -- S$1.50 at a Participating Store`)'s `points per dollar` EQUALS 3
#ASSERT (`the rate on` `POSB PAssion Debit` `a PAssion cardmember, registered and linked` `a month with nothing spent yet` `PAssion cl.10 -- S$1.50 at a Participating Store`)'s `earns the bonus rate` EQUALS FALSE

-- cl.3, verbatim: "The Promotion is valid from 1 October 2023 to 30 September
-- 2025 ('Promotion Period')." That date is in the past, and the domain names
-- this document as the `Source expired` case in terms. The assertion is
-- therefore on the DOCUMENT's currency, not the transaction's: if it fails
-- because the encoding dates the status to the transaction instead, that is
-- worth knowing and is a finding, not a reason to relax the assertion.
#ASSERT (`the rate on` `POSB PAssion Debit` `a PAssion cardmember, registered and linked` `a month with nothing spent yet` `PAssion cl.10 -- S$1.50 at a Participating Store`)'s status EQUALS `Source expired`

-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
-- posb-passion-yuu-tnc cl.6, verbatim:
--
--   Awarding type      | Accelerator
--   Base Points        | 1.5% cash rebates (3X yuu Points)
--   POSB Bonus Points  | 7.5% cash rebates (15X yuu Points)
--
-- with cl.8(a): "Cardmember can earn 15X yuu Points when Cardmember meets all
-- the following Qualified Spend criteria within each Qualifying month i. At
-- least S$300 total spend at Participating Stores ii. At least S$400 total
-- spend at non-Participating Stores".
--
-- 3 + 15 = 18 yuu Points per S$1, and 18 x 0.5% = 9% -- which is the figure
-- in the document's OWN TITLE: "Up to 9% Cash Rebates (18X yuu Points)
-- Promotion". The title is the worked example here, and it settles for
-- PAssion the adding-versus-replacing question that dbs-yuu-card-tnc cl.7
-- leaves open.
--
-- cl.8(b): "Capped at a maximum of S$25 cash rebate (5,000 yuu Points) to be
-- awarded per Cardmember per Qualifying Month". Stated in points against the
-- 15X bonus rate, so the dollars of bonus-earning spend is not a figure the
-- document gives. cl.8(e)'s table runs its Qualifying Months from the 1st to
-- the month end ("1 to 30 Sep 2024", "1 to 31 Oct 2024", ...), which is a
-- calendar month.
-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
GIVETH A Transaction
`PAssion cl.8 -- S$50 at a Participating Store` MEANS Transaction WITH
    `merchant name`                IS "Giant"
    `merchant`                     IS Giant
    `merchant category code`       IS 5411
    `transaction description`      IS "GIANT"
    `description patterns`         IS EMPTY
    `charge kind`                  IS `Retail purchase`
    `amount`                       IS 50
    `currency`                     IS "SGD"
    `posted in a foreign currency` IS FALSE
    `transaction date`             IS YMD 2025 9 15
    `posting date`                 IS YMD 2025 9 16
    `payment channel`              IS `Tapped at a terminal`
    `credential`                   IS `The physical card`
    `merchant indicator`           IS Unknown
    `made in Singapore`            IS TRUE

#ASSERT (`the rate on` `POSB PAssion Debit` `a PAssion cardmember, registered and linked` `a month meeting both PAssion thresholds` `PAssion cl.8 -- S$50 at a Participating Store`)'s `points per dollar` EQUALS 18
#ASSERT (`the rate on` `POSB PAssion Debit` `a PAssion cardmember, registered and linked` `a month meeting both PAssion thresholds` `PAssion cl.8 -- S$50 at a Participating Store`)'s `earns the bonus rate` EQUALS TRUE
#ASSERT (`the rate on` `POSB PAssion Debit` `a PAssion cardmember, registered and linked` `a month meeting both PAssion thresholds` `PAssion cl.8 -- S$50 at a Participating Store`)'s cap's capped EQUALS TRUE
#ASSERT (`the rate on` `POSB PAssion Debit` `a PAssion cardmember, registered and linked` `a month meeting both PAssion thresholds` `PAssion cl.8 -- S$50 at a Participating Store`)'s cap's basis EQUALS `Calendar month`
#ASSERT (`the rate on` `POSB PAssion Debit` `a PAssion cardmember, registered and linked` `a month with nothing spent yet` `PAssion cl.8 -- S$50 at a Participating Store`)'s `points per dollar` EQUALS 3

-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
-- posb-passion-yuu-tnc cl.7(d) and cl.8(d), verbatim and identical in both:
-- "Retail transactions made at the Participating Merchants located outside of
-- Singapore and/or charged in foreign currencies are not eligible for this
-- Promotion." cl.4 says the same from the other side: Qualified Spend
-- "includes only retail transactions ... that are in local currency".
--
-- Asserted on the bonus only. The clauses also take away the 3X base, but
-- what such a charge earns INSTEAD is in the DBS Debit Card Agreement, which
-- this corpus does not hold -- so the residual rate is not something this
-- document determines and is not asserted.
-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
GIVETH A Transaction
`PAssion cl.7(d) -- a Participating Store abroad, in foreign currency` MEANS Transaction WITH
    `merchant name`                IS "Guardian"
    `merchant`                     IS Guardian
    `merchant category code`       IS 5912
    `transaction description`      IS "GUARDIAN MY"
    `description patterns`         IS EMPTY
    `charge kind`                  IS `Retail purchase`
    `amount`                       IS 40
    `currency`                     IS "MYR"
    `posted in a foreign currency` IS TRUE
    `transaction date`             IS YMD 2025 9 15
    `posting date`                 IS YMD 2025 9 16
    `payment channel`              IS `Tapped at a terminal`
    `credential`                   IS `The physical card`
    `merchant indicator`           IS Unknown
    `made in Singapore`            IS FALSE

#ASSERT (`the rate on` `POSB PAssion Debit` `a PAssion cardmember, registered and linked` `a month meeting both PAssion thresholds` `PAssion cl.7(d) -- a Participating Store abroad, in foreign currency`)'s `earns the bonus rate` EQUALS FALSE


§§ `UOB Lady's Solitaire`

-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
-- uob-ladys-faq Q9, verbatim: "How do I earn 10X UNI$ per S$5 spent
-- (equivalent to 4 miles per S$1)? You will earn 10X UNI$ per S$5 spent based
-- on the preferred rewards category(ies) chosen for the current calendar
-- quarter."
--
-- The FAQ's heading states a RATE and its miles equivalent in one line, and
-- the T&C derives it: cl.2(b) "Base UNI$ means the reward of UNI$1 for every
-- S$5.00 spent (equivalent to 0.4 miles per S$1 spent)"; cl.2(c) "Bonus UNI$
-- means the bonus reward of 9X UNI$ per S$5 spent (equivalent to 3.6 miles
-- per S$1 spent)"; cl.3 "UNI$ can be converted to KrisFlyer or Asia miles ...
-- at the conversion rate of UNI$1 = 2 miles".
--
-- In the domain's per-DOLLAR unit that is 10 UNI$ / S$5 = 2 UNI$ per S$1, and
-- 2 x 2 = 4 miles per S$1, which is the figure in the FAQ's own heading. UOB
-- is one of only two cards in this corpus whose miles conversion is stated in
-- a document we hold.
--
-- uob-ladys-faq Q17's table gives Dining as MCC "5811, 5812, 5814, 5499", so
-- a restaurant at 5812 is inside a Dining election.
-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
GIVETH A Transaction
`UOB FAQ Q9 -- S$100 at a restaurant, MCC 5812` MEANS Transaction WITH
    `merchant name`                IS "A restaurant"
    `merchant`                     IS `Another merchant`
    `merchant category code`       IS 5812
    `transaction description`      IS "RESTAURANT"
    `description patterns`         IS EMPTY
    `charge kind`                  IS `Retail purchase`
    `amount`                       IS 100
    `currency`                     IS "SGD"
    `posted in a foreign currency` IS FALSE
    `transaction date`             IS YMD 2026 9 10
    `posting date`                 IS YMD 2026 9 11
    `payment channel`              IS `Inserted or swiped at a terminal`
    `credential`                   IS `The physical card`
    `merchant indicator`           IS Unknown
    `made in Singapore`            IS TRUE

#ASSERT (`the rate on` `UOB Lady's Solitaire` `a Solitaire cardmember electing Dining and Family` `a month with nothing spent yet` `UOB FAQ Q9 -- S$100 at a restaurant, MCC 5812`)'s `points per dollar` EQUALS 2
#ASSERT (`the rate on` `UOB Lady's Solitaire` `a Solitaire cardmember electing Dining and Family` `a month with nothing spent yet` `UOB FAQ Q9 -- S$100 at a restaurant, MCC 5812`)'s `miles per point` EQUALS 2
#ASSERT (`the rate on` `UOB Lady's Solitaire` `a Solitaire cardmember electing Dining and Family` `a month with nothing spent yet` `UOB FAQ Q9 -- S$100 at a restaurant, MCC 5812`)'s `miles per dollar` EQUALS 4
#ASSERT (`the rate on` `UOB Lady's Solitaire` `a Solitaire cardmember electing Dining and Family` `a month with nothing spent yet` `UOB FAQ Q9 -- S$100 at a restaurant, MCC 5812`)'s `earns the bonus rate` EQUALS TRUE
#ASSERT (`the rate on` `UOB Lady's Solitaire` `a Solitaire cardmember electing Dining and Family` `a month with nothing spent yet` `UOB FAQ Q9 -- S$100 at a restaurant, MCC 5812`)'s `conversion status` EQUALS Verified

-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
-- uob-ladys-cards-tnc cl.6(b), the Note and the illustration beneath it,
-- verbatim: "With effect from 1 August 2025, if you hold a Lady's Solitaire
-- Card, 2,700 UNI$ (which is equivalent to S$1,500 spent), with each
-- Preferred Rewards Category capped at 1,350 UNI$ (which is equivalent to
-- S$750 spent). ... For illustration purposes, if you have selected only one
-- Preferred Rewards Category, you can earn up to 1,350 UNI$ per calendar
-- month on that selected Preferred Rewards Category. If you have selected two
-- Preferred Rewards Categories, you can earn up to 1,350 UNI$ on each of your
-- two selected Preferred Rewards Categories."
--
-- uob-ladys-faq Q7 says the same thing the other way round: "If you would
-- prefer to choose only one preferred rewards category ... you will only be
-- able to earn bonus 9X UNI$ on up to S$750 in spending on that rewards
-- category per calendar month. If you have selected two preferred rewards
-- categories, you will be able to earn bonus 9X UNI$ on up to S$750 spent per
-- preferred rewards category per calendar month."
--
-- The illustration's point is that S$750 is PER CATEGORY and does not move
-- when a cardmember elects one category instead of two -- so the two
-- assertions differ only in the cardholder, and both expect 750. The
-- card-level 2,700 UNI$ / S$1,500 figure is the sum of two such pots and is
-- not what a single transaction runs against.
--
-- The document checks its own arithmetic: 1,350 UNI$ at cl.2(c)'s 9 UNI$ per
-- S$5 = 1.8 UNI$ per S$1 gives 1,350 / 1.8 = S$750.
--
-- cl.8: "any Base UNI$ and Bonus UNI$ that may be awarded ... will be
-- computed based on the date that the transaction is posted on UOB's
-- systems", and uob-ladys-faq Q11 agrees: "The bonus UNI$ will be calculated
-- based on the posting date of the qualifying transactions."
-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
#ASSERT (`the rate on` `UOB Lady's Solitaire` `a Solitaire cardmember electing Dining only` `a month with nothing spent yet` `UOB FAQ Q9 -- S$100 at a restaurant, MCC 5812`)'s cap's `bonus spend per month` EQUALS 750
#ASSERT (`the rate on` `UOB Lady's Solitaire` `a Solitaire cardmember electing Dining only` `a month with nothing spent yet` `UOB FAQ Q9 -- S$100 at a restaurant, MCC 5812`)'s cap's capped EQUALS TRUE
#ASSERT (`the rate on` `UOB Lady's Solitaire` `a Solitaire cardmember electing Dining only` `a month with nothing spent yet` `UOB FAQ Q9 -- S$100 at a restaurant, MCC 5812`)'s cap's basis EQUALS `Calendar month`
#ASSERT (`the rate on` `UOB Lady's Solitaire` `a Solitaire cardmember electing Dining only` `a month with nothing spent yet` `UOB FAQ Q9 -- S$100 at a restaurant, MCC 5812`)'s cap's attribution EQUALS `By posting date`
#ASSERT (`the rate on` `UOB Lady's Solitaire` `a Solitaire cardmember electing Dining and Family` `a month with nothing spent yet` `UOB FAQ Q9 -- S$100 at a restaurant, MCC 5812`)'s cap's `bonus spend per month` EQUALS 750
#ASSERT (`the rate on` `UOB Lady's Solitaire` `a Solitaire cardmember electing Dining and Family` `a month with nothing spent yet` `UOB FAQ Q9 -- S$100 at a restaurant, MCC 5812`)'s cap's attribution EQUALS `By posting date`

-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
-- uob-ladys-faq Q10, verbatim: "Will I earn UNI$ if I do not choose my
-- Preferred Rewards Category(ies) to earn 10X UNI$? You will not earn the
-- bonus 9X UNI$ on every S$5 spent if you do not choose your preferred
-- rewards category(ies). However, you can continue to earn a base of UNI$1
-- for every S$5 spent on your UOB Lady's Card."
--
-- UNI$1 per S$5 = 0.2 UNI$ per S$1, and at cl.3's UNI$1 = 2 miles that is 0.4
-- miles per S$1 -- cl.2(b)'s own parenthesis. Same charge as Q9 above; only
-- the election changes.
-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
#ASSERT (`the rate on` `UOB Lady's Solitaire` `a Solitaire cardmember who elected nothing` `a month with nothing spent yet` `UOB FAQ Q9 -- S$100 at a restaurant, MCC 5812`)'s `points per dollar` EQUALS 0.2
#ASSERT (`the rate on` `UOB Lady's Solitaire` `a Solitaire cardmember who elected nothing` `a month with nothing spent yet` `UOB FAQ Q9 -- S$100 at a restaurant, MCC 5812`)'s `miles per dollar` EQUALS 0.4
#ASSERT (`the rate on` `UOB Lady's Solitaire` `a Solitaire cardmember who elected nothing` `a month with nothing spent yet` `UOB FAQ Q9 -- S$100 at a restaurant, MCC 5812`)'s `earns the bonus rate` EQUALS FALSE

-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
