§§ `DBS Woman's World`

-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
-- dbs-womans-card-tnc cl.16, verbatim: "The mechanics of the awarding and
-- calculation of DBS Points is illustrated in the table below.
--
--   Rewards                          | For every S$5 spend | Points Awarded On
--   Base Rewards - All Spend         | 1X DBS Point        | Next working day
--   Bonus Rewards - Overseas Spend   | Additional 2X DBS Points | Next working day
--   Bonus Rewards - Online Spend     | Additional 9X DBS Points for local spend
--                                    | Additional 7X DBS Points for overseas spend
--                                    | Next calendar month"
--
-- Four rows, four cases, and the table's own arithmetic makes the four land
-- on three rates per S$1 (the domain's unit, so each figure is the table's
-- "per S$5" divided by 5):
--
--   local, not online    1X            / 5 = 0.2 DBS Points per S$1
--   overseas, not online (1 + 2)X      / 5 = 0.6
--   local, online        (1 + 9)X      / 5 = 2
--   overseas, online     (1 + 2 + 7)X  / 5 = 2
--
-- The last two matching is the reason the table prints 7X for overseas online
-- and 9X for local: both paths arrive at 10X per S$5.
--
-- cl.11 defines online spend as "retail transaction for goods and services
-- made via the Internet and processed by the respective merchants/acquirers
-- as an online transaction through Mastercard Worldwide networks", and cl.13
-- says who decides that: "DBS determines an online transaction based on
-- system indicators. These indicators are decided by the merchant and their
-- banker, and passed to DBS when the transaction is posted to the Card." So
-- the online rows state a channel outcome and the fixtures carry the
-- indicator the row is about.
--
-- cl.12: "'Overseas spend' refers to retail transactions for goods and
-- services posted in foreign currencies (other than Singapore dollars)" --
-- which is why the overseas fixtures turn `posted in a foreign currency` on
-- rather than relying on where the cardmember was standing.
--
-- NO MILES ASSERTIONS HERE. This T&C states no conversion from DBS Points to
-- miles; cl.6 defers to the DBS Rewards Programme Terms and Conditions, which
-- this corpus does not hold. Asserting a miles figure would be asserting
-- something no held document says.
-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
GIVETH A Transaction
`Woman's cl.16 -- a local charge the acquirer flags card-present` MEANS Transaction WITH
    `merchant name`                IS "A restaurant"
    `merchant`                     IS `Another merchant`
    `merchant category code`       IS 5812
    `transaction description`      IS "RESTAURANT"
    `description patterns`         IS EMPTY
    `charge kind`                  IS `Retail purchase`
    `amount`                       IS 100
    `currency`                     IS "SGD"
    `posted in a foreign currency` IS FALSE
    `transaction date`             IS YMD 2026 9 10
    `posting date`                 IS YMD 2026 9 11
    `payment channel`              IS `Inserted or swiped at a terminal`
    `credential`                   IS `The physical card`
    `merchant indicator`           IS `Flags card-present`
    `made in Singapore`            IS TRUE

#ASSERT (`the rate on` `DBS Woman's World` `a DBS Woman's World cardmember` `a month with nothing spent yet` `Woman's cl.16 -- a local charge the acquirer flags card-present`)'s `points per dollar` EQUALS 0.2
#ASSERT (`the rate on` `DBS Woman's World` `a DBS Woman's World cardmember` `a month with nothing spent yet` `Woman's cl.16 -- a local charge the acquirer flags card-present`)'s `earns the bonus rate` EQUALS FALSE

GIVETH A Transaction
`Woman's cl.16 -- a local charge the acquirer flags online` MEANS Transaction WITH
    `merchant name`                IS "An online retailer"
    `merchant`                     IS `Another merchant`
    `merchant category code`       IS 5732
    `transaction description`      IS "ONLINE RETAILER"
    `description patterns`         IS EMPTY
    `charge kind`                  IS `Retail purchase`
    `amount`                       IS 100
    `currency`                     IS "SGD"
    `posted in a foreign currency` IS FALSE
    `transaction date`             IS YMD 2026 9 10
    `posting date`                 IS YMD 2026 9 11
    `payment channel`              IS `Paid in a website or app`
    `credential`                   IS `The physical card`
    `merchant indicator`           IS `Flags online`
    `made in Singapore`            IS TRUE

#ASSERT (`the rate on` `DBS Woman's World` `a DBS Woman's World cardmember` `a month with nothing spent yet` `Woman's cl.16 -- a local charge the acquirer flags online`)'s `points per dollar` EQUALS 2
#ASSERT (`the rate on` `DBS Woman's World` `a DBS Woman's World cardmember` `a month with nothing spent yet` `Woman's cl.16 -- a local charge the acquirer flags online`)'s `earns the bonus rate` EQUALS TRUE

-- cl.19(b): "Online spend will be accumulated for the month and awarded bonus
-- points in the following calendar month, capped at the first S$1,000 of
-- online spend per calendar month." cl.19(c): "Online spend must be charged to
-- your card within the calendar month, based on transaction date" -- DBS
-- attributes by transaction date where UOB attributes by posting date, which
-- is why the domain keeps them as two independent axes.
#ASSERT (`the rate on` `DBS Woman's World` `a DBS Woman's World cardmember` `a month with nothing spent yet` `Woman's cl.16 -- a local charge the acquirer flags online`)'s cap's capped EQUALS TRUE
#ASSERT (`the rate on` `DBS Woman's World` `a DBS Woman's World cardmember` `a month with nothing spent yet` `Woman's cl.16 -- a local charge the acquirer flags online`)'s cap's `bonus spend per month` EQUALS 1000
#ASSERT (`the rate on` `DBS Woman's World` `a DBS Woman's World cardmember` `a month with nothing spent yet` `Woman's cl.16 -- a local charge the acquirer flags online`)'s cap's basis EQUALS `Calendar month`
#ASSERT (`the rate on` `DBS Woman's World` `a DBS Woman's World cardmember` `a month with nothing spent yet` `Woman's cl.16 -- a local charge the acquirer flags online`)'s cap's attribution EQUALS `By transaction date`

GIVETH A Transaction
`Woman's cl.16 -- an overseas charge, not online` MEANS Transaction WITH
    `merchant name`                IS "A department store in Tokyo"
    `merchant`                     IS `Another merchant`
    `merchant category code`       IS 5311
    `transaction description`      IS "TOKYO DEPT STORE"
    `description patterns`         IS EMPTY
    `charge kind`                  IS `Retail purchase`
    `amount`                       IS 300
    `currency`                     IS "JPY"
    `posted in a foreign currency` IS TRUE
    `transaction date`             IS YMD 2026 9 10
    `posting date`                 IS YMD 2026 9 12
    `payment channel`              IS `Inserted or swiped at a terminal`
    `credential`                   IS `The physical card`
    `merchant indicator`           IS `Flags card-present`
    `made in Singapore`            IS FALSE

#ASSERT (`the rate on` `DBS Woman's World` `a DBS Woman's World cardmember` `a month with nothing spent yet` `Woman's cl.16 -- an overseas charge, not online`)'s `points per dollar` EQUALS 0.6
#ASSERT (`the rate on` `DBS Woman's World` `a DBS Woman's World cardmember` `a month with nothing spent yet` `Woman's cl.16 -- an overseas charge, not online`)'s `earns the bonus rate` EQUALS TRUE

GIVETH A Transaction
`Woman's cl.16 -- an overseas charge the acquirer flags online` MEANS Transaction WITH
    `merchant name`                IS "An overseas online retailer"
    `merchant`                     IS `Another merchant`
    `merchant category code`       IS 5732
    `transaction description`      IS "OVERSEAS ONLINE"
    `description patterns`         IS EMPTY
    `charge kind`                  IS `Retail purchase`
    `amount`                       IS 300
    `currency`                     IS "USD"
    `posted in a foreign currency` IS TRUE
    `transaction date`             IS YMD 2026 9 10
    `posting date`                 IS YMD 2026 9 12
    `payment channel`              IS `Paid in a website or app`
    `credential`                   IS `The physical card`
    `merchant indicator`           IS `Flags online`
    `made in Singapore`            IS FALSE

#ASSERT (`the rate on` `DBS Woman's World` `a DBS Woman's World cardmember` `a month with nothing spent yet` `Woman's cl.16 -- an overseas charge the acquirer flags online`)'s `points per dollar` EQUALS 2
#ASSERT (`the rate on` `DBS Woman's World` `a DBS Woman's World cardmember` `a month with nothing spent yet` `Woman's cl.16 -- an overseas charge the acquirer flags online`)'s `earns the bonus rate` EQUALS TRUE

-- cl.13 again, from the cardholder's side: the indicator is the merchant's to
-- decide and is latent at the moment of payment. The same charge as the two
