    `charge kind`                  IS `Retail purchase`
    `amount`                       IS 100
    `currency`                     IS "SGD"
    `posted in a foreign currency` IS FALSE
    `transaction date`             IS YMD 2026 9 10
    `posting date`                 IS YMD 2026 9 11
    `payment channel`              IS `Paid in a website or app`
    `credential`                   IS `The physical card`
    `merchant indicator`           IS Unknown
    `made in Singapore`            IS TRUE

#ASSERT (`the rate on` `DBS Woman's World` `a DBS Woman's World cardmember` `a month with nothing spent yet` `Woman's cl.13 -- a local charge whose indicator is not known`)'s `depends on the merchant indicator` EQUALS TRUE


§§ `Where a FAQ and its own T&C disagree`

-- ===========================================================================
-- TWO CONFLICTS, AND WHY THEY ARE ASSERTED THE WAY THEY ARE.
--
-- Each assertion below states what the T&C says, because the T&C is the
-- contract and the FAQ is a description of it. Both are written so that an
-- encoding which later follows the FAQ instead -- by a well-meant edit, or by
-- a reading of a redrafted clause -- FAILS here rather than passing quietly.
-- The comment on each says what the FAQ would have given, so a reader who
-- trips one can see immediately which way the encoding moved.
-- ===========================================================================

-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
-- CONFLICT 1 -- hsbc-revolution-faq Q2 against hsbc-revolution-reward-points-tnc
-- cl.5, cl.7 and cl.7.1.
--
-- The FAQ, verbatim: "The following transactions that fall within the list of
-- Merchant Category Codes (MCC) below, qualify for 10x Reward points: ...
-- transactions made via contactless payments (payWave, Apple Pay and Google
-- Pay payment methods). With effect from 15 July 2024, contactless payment
-- transactions will earn 1 HSBC Reward point."
--
-- The T&C, verbatim, cl.5: "'Selected Contactless Payments' refers to
-- Qualifying Transactions made via Visa contactless through a contactless
-- terminal mode which includes Visa payWave, Apple Pay, Google Pay and
-- Samsung Pay." cl.7: "'Eligible Transactions' refers to Selected Contactless
-- Payments and Selected Online Transactions that fall within any one of the
-- following MCCs". cl.7.1: "(i) 1 Reward point ('Base Points') for every SGD1
-- of the Eligible Transaction; and (ii)(a) 9 Reward points ('Bonus Points')
-- for every SGD1 of the Eligible Transaction".
--
-- SO: 10 Reward points per SGD1 under the T&C, 1 under the FAQ. The T&C
-- governs, and it is also the LATER document -- it carries "Effective from 1
-- April 2026" on every page, where the FAQ's carve-out is dated 15 July 2024.
-- A contactless tap at an in-list MCC is therefore still a 10X charge.
--
-- MCC 5942 (Book Stores) is row 27 of cl.7's table. The credential is an
-- Apple Pay token, which cl.5 names, and the indicator is `Flags card-present`
-- because cl.5's subject is a charge taken through a contactless TERMINAL --
-- the one place in this suite where an example states card-present and the
-- bonus is earned anyway.
-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
GIVETH A Transaction
`HSBC conflict -- an Apple Pay tap at a bookshop, MCC 5942` MEANS Transaction WITH
    `merchant name`                IS "A bookshop"
    `merchant`                     IS `Another merchant`
    `merchant category code`       IS 5942
    `transaction description`      IS "BOOKSHOP"
    `description patterns`         IS EMPTY
    `charge kind`                  IS `Retail purchase`
    `amount`                       IS 60
    `currency`                     IS "SGD"
    `posted in a foreign currency` IS FALSE
    `transaction date`             IS YMD 2026 9 10
    `posting date`                 IS YMD 2026 9 11
    `payment channel`              IS `Tapped at a terminal`
    `credential`                   IS `A mobile wallet token`
    `merchant indicator`           IS `Flags card-present`
    `made in Singapore`            IS TRUE

-- T&C cl.7.1: 1 + 9 = 10. FAQ Q2 would give 1. If this ever reads 1, the
-- encoding has followed the FAQ over its own contract.
#ASSERT (`the rate on` `HSBC Revolution` `an HSBC cardholder below the deposits tier` `a month with nothing spent yet` `HSBC conflict -- an Apple Pay tap at a bookshop, MCC 5942`)'s `points per dollar` EQUALS 10
#ASSERT (`the rate on` `HSBC Revolution` `an HSBC cardholder below the deposits tier` `a month with nothing spent yet` `HSBC conflict -- an Apple Pay tap at a bookshop, MCC 5942`)'s `earns the bonus rate` EQUALS TRUE

-- cl.7.1(ii)(b) applies to a contactless Eligible Transaction exactly as it
-- does to an online one, so the deposits tier doubles this charge too: 20.
-- Under the FAQ's reading there would be no bonus to raise and the tier would
-- make no difference at all, so this assertion trips on the same defect from
-- a second direction.
#ASSERT (`the rate on` `HSBC Revolution` `an HSBC cardholder at the deposits tier` `a month with nothing spent yet` `HSBC conflict -- an Apple Pay tap at a bookshop, MCC 5942`)'s `points per dollar` EQUALS 20

-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
-- CONFLICT 2 -- citi-rewards-10x-faq Q1's travel footnote against
-- citi-rewards-10x-tnc cl.6's travel footnote.
--
-- The two footnotes are word-for-word identical until their last six words.
--
-- The FAQ, Q1, verbatim: "*For clarity, travel-related transactions refer to
-- transactions which are either wholly or partially related to any form of
-- travel, whether local or overseas and include but are not limited to
-- transactions that fall within the following MCCs (i.e. any transactions at
-- merchants with the following MCCs will not be a QUALIFYING CHARGE)".
--
-- The T&C, cl.6, verbatim: "... (i.e. any transactions at merchants with the
-- following MCCs will not be a 10X POINTS ELIGIBLE TRANSACTION)".
--
-- Those are different exclusions and they differ by a whole base point.
-- "Qualifying Charge" is the T&C's cl.5 term for a charge that earns anything
-- at all; "10X Points Eligible Transaction" is cl.6's term for one that earns
-- the bonus. Under the FAQ a hotel booking earns NOTHING. Under the T&C it is
-- still a Qualifying Charge -- cl.5's own exclusion list does not mention
-- travel, and neither does citi-rewards-exclusion-list, which cl.5(xii)
-- incorporates -- so cl.12 applies: "Eligible Cardholders will earn 1 Base
-- Point for every S$1 of Qualifying Charges (which are not 10X Points
-- Eligible Transactions)".
--
-- SO: 1 Point per S$1 under the T&C, 0 under the FAQ. MCC 7011 (Lodging --
-- Hotels, Motels, Resorts, Not Elsewhere Classified) is in both footnotes'
-- tables. The charge is made online, so the cl.6(ii) limb would otherwise
-- have fired and the footnote is doing real work.
-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
GIVETH A Transaction
`Citi conflict -- an online hotel booking, MCC 7011` MEANS Transaction WITH
    `merchant name`                IS "A hotel"
    `merchant`                     IS `Another merchant`
    `merchant category code`       IS 7011
    `transaction description`      IS "HOTEL BOOKING"
    `description patterns`         IS EMPTY
    `charge kind`                  IS `Retail purchase`
    `amount`                       IS 450
    `currency`                     IS "SGD"
    `posted in a foreign currency` IS FALSE
    `transaction date`             IS YMD 2026 9 10
    `posting date`                 IS YMD 2026 9 11
    `payment channel`              IS `Paid in a website or app`
    `credential`                   IS `The physical card`
    `merchant indicator`           IS `Flags online`
    `made in Singapore`            IS TRUE

-- T&C cl.12: 1 Base Point per S$1. FAQ Q1's footnote would give 0. A reading
-- of 0 here means the encoding has taken the FAQ's wider exclusion.
#ASSERT (`the rate on` `Citi Rewards` `a Citi Rewards cardholder` `a month with nothing spent yet` `Citi conflict -- an online hotel booking, MCC 7011`)'s `points per dollar` EQUALS 1
-- And the footnote's actual job, on which FAQ and T&C agree: no 10X.
#ASSERT (`the rate on` `Citi Rewards` `a Citi Rewards cardholder` `a month with nothing spent yet` `Citi conflict -- an online hotel booking, MCC 7011`)'s `earns the bonus rate` EQUALS FALSE
